        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "67ecb720-d66b-552e-9cfc-bee2a7e3447a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Isaak Dunayevsky, Grigori Aleksandrov, Sergey Agranyan, Mark Lisyansky\n- Roles: film composer, conductor, film director, lyricists\n- Works: Moya Moskva\n- Topics: Soviet film, operetta, film comedies\n\nFacts:\n- Isaak Osipovich Dunayevsky was born on 30 January 1900 and died on 25 July 1955.\n- Grigori Vasilyevich Aleksandrov was born on 23 January 1903 and died on 16 December 1983.\n- Isaak Dunayevsky was a Soviet film composer and conductor of the 1930s and 1940s.\n- Isaak Dunayevsky achieved major success in music for operetta and film comedies.\n- Isaak Dunayevsky frequently worked with Soviet film director Grigori Aleksandrov.\n- In 1941, Isaak Dunayevsky composed the music for Moya Moskva.\n- In 1941, Sergey Agranyan and Mark Lisyansky wrote the lyrics for Moya Moskva.\n- Grigori Aleksandrov was a prominent Soviet film director.\n- Grigori Aleksandrov was named a People's Artist of the USSR in 1947.\n- Grigori Aleksandrov was named a Hero of Socialist Labor in 1973.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
